WEBVTT

00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:02.204
Memories are encoded most strongly
when we're paying attention,

00:02:02.246 --> 00:02:06.579
when we're deeply engaged,
and when information is meaningful to us.

00:02:06.621 --> 00:02:10.038
Mental and physical health problems,
which tend to increase as we age,

00:02:10.079 --> 00:02:12.163
interfere with our ability
to pay attention,

00:02:12.204 --> 00:02:14.788
and thus act as memory thieves.

00:02:14.829 --> 00:02:18.496
Another leading cause of memory 
problems is chronic stress.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:22.038
When we’re constantly overloaded
with work and personal responsibilities,

00:02:22.079 --> 00:02:24.371
our bodies are on hyperalert.

00:02:24.413 --> 00:02:27.288
This response has evolved
from the physiological mechanism

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:30.538
designed to make sure
we can survive in a crisis.